EXP-0060 postmortem — DLSS -> arg10, black flash persists (2026-10-28 18:32–18:34)
source: E:\LeviLauncher\versions\1.26.51.01-r3\logs\latest.log
raw excerpt: docs/agent/evidence/arg10-dlss-EXP-0060.log

User report (verbatim)
"这次抖动没有复现，黑色闪动依然存在，并且隐约看出可能不是全屏黑而是部分黑
（此为疑问点，可能是视觉暂留）"

What the log shows
- `[vvsr] sr arg10 #600` … `#6000`: 11 periodic lines — the DLSS evaluate + PS path
  ran thousands of times.
- `inject fixed`: only 4 lines; `arg10 writer not found`: 51 lines.
  So most of those evaluate calls were on submissions that were never injected.
- The world frames in this session are 70/71-list; the writer was not found there,
  while a 50-list submission did inject (`k=29/50 injected=120`).

Root causes
1. record-before-boundary. `prepare()` ran `record()` (which evaluates DLSS) before
   it decided the cut. On UI/other submissions the feature's history was advanced
   with a frame that never reached the screen; the next world frame then reprojected
   against a wrong history — a one-frame corruption, consistent with a brief black
   (possibly partial) flash. Fix: check `arg10WriterSplit` before `record()`; on a
   miss return without evaluating. Also set a gap flag and Reset the DLSS history on
   the first injected frame after a world miss.
2. list-level DSV filter too coarse. The writer search required `!sig->dsv`, but
   `dsv` is sticky for the whole list: a list that binds depth anywhere is rejected
   even when its arg10 binding is a no-DSV call. The 70-list world writer was lost
   this way. Fix: the arg10 binding itself is the criterion; drop `!dsv`.

Not established
- Full-screen vs partial black: no frame capture and no reproducible trigger. If it
  persists after the two fixes, capture the trigger and a frame range before adding
  another patch.
